Z||000000||firstfiero||12-22-2001||10:57 AM||||     My mecnanic can't find a bracket for my slave cylinder. He can get one off a 4 cylinder but doesn't know if they are the same. Can you use a 4 cylinder bracket on the v6? If you can't anyone have a bracket they can sell me.   As always thanks for your help.<P>------------------<BR><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Rodney||12-22-2001||11:09 AM||||I have reproduced this bracket in steel. <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com/transaxle.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.rodneydickman.com/transaxle.html</A> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||firstfiero||12-22-2001||11:17 AM||||    Thanks Rodney but with christmas and tax time here I'd prefer not to pay 75 bucks for the bracket. this job is going to be expensive enough as it is. All though I'm sure your part would far exceed the quality of a gm part. Anyone with a parts car?<P>------------------<BR><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||1
